{
"dur": 38.099,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 8.078,
"text": "In 1796 he took over a hungry, ragged army in Italy. In about a year, he beat Austrian army after Austrian army.",
"end": 8.353
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 8.353,
"vo_start": 8.628,
"vo_end": 16.824,
"text": "In 1798 he sailed to Egypt with an army and over a hundred and fifty scientists. But the British navy destroyed his fleet, and his army was trapped.",
"end": 17.099
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 17.099,
"vo_start": 17.374,
"vo_end": 22.729,
"text": "So he left his army behind, slipped back to France, and told everyone it was a triumph.",
"end": 23.004
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 23.004,
"vo_start": 23.279,
"vo_end": 28.839,
"text": "In November 1799, he seized power with soldiers. He was thirty and ran France.",
"end": 29.114
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 29.114,
"vo_start": 29.389,
"vo_end": 37.149,
"text": "On the second of December 1804, in Notre-Dame, the Pope came to crown him. Napoleon took the crown and put it on his own head.",
"end": 38.099
}
],
